                <pb facs="0178" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg94"/>

                <head>No. 59.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 30,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch No. 132, of
                    April 19, 1886, touching the claim of Mr. John P. Cowles, jr., for reduction of
                    duty on damaged exports, and have to approve your precautionary note to the
                    Yamên of December 13 last, in such cases.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
